msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: konfigurator.docbook:1512
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the <guilabel>Packers</guilabel> tab you will see a list of archive formats. Some are filled and some are empty. The ones that are available (filled) are supported by &krusader;. For them, &krusader; will handle the archives transparently and let you open them as folders (provided you have checked the <guilabel>Browse Archives As Folders</guilabel> item in the <link linkend=\"konfig-archives\">Archives</link> section); otherwise, &krusader; will attempt to invoke an application which opens archives of that type. If a certain archive item is empty, it means that &krusader; could not find the appropriate executables in the configured path. The next archives are supported: ace, arj, bzip2, deb, gzip, iso, lha, lzma, rar, rpm, tar, xz, zip and 7z."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable5
#: konfigurator.docbook:1496
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the <guilabel>Packers</guilabel> tab you will see a list of archive formats. Some are filled and some are empty. The ones that are available (filled) are supported by &krusader;. For them, &krusader; will handle the archives transparently and let you open them as folders (provided you have checked the <guilabel>Browse Archives As Directories</guilabel> item in the <link linkend=\"konfig-archives\">Archives</link> section); otherwise, &krusader; will attempt to invoke an application which opens archives of that type. If a certain archive item is empty, it means that &krusader; could not find the appropriate executables in the configured path. The next archives are supported: ace, arj, bzip2, deb, gzip, iso, lha, lzma, rar, rpm, tar, xz, zip and 7z."
msgstr ""

